          "id": "block_1",
          "text": "Menahem gives Pul silver so that Assyrian support will confirm his rule (vv. 19-20). That makes this payment a calculated effort to secure his kingdom, but tribute should not automatically be treated as evidence for one fixed kind of relationship or a ruler's complete motives. Elsewhere in Kings, payments and refusals of tribute serve different political and literary functions.",
