        {
          "id": "block_2",
          "text": "Tiglath-pileser's capture of northern Israelite places and deportation of their inhabitants is a major loss in this chapter (v. 29), but it should not be compressed into every later stage of Israel's downfall. Kings presents territorial loss, Samaria's siege, deportation, and later resettlement through several notices; distinguishing those stages keeps this verse from being made to carry the whole later history at once.",
